2. ROS 2 Nodes & Their Responsibilities
#	Node (Package)	Type (Lifecycle / Composable)	Main Responsibility
1	map_server (nav2_map_server)	Lifecycle	Loads the static occupancy grid (.yaml/.pgm) and serves /map.
2	amcl (nav2_amcl)	Lifecycle	Particle filter localization using /scan + /odom → publishes /amcl_pose and /particlecloud.
3	laser_filter_node (laser_filters)	Composable	Optionally filters raw LiDAR (/scan) (e.g., noise, min/max range, angle clipping).
4	sensor_fusion (robot_localization)	Lifecycle	Fuses wheel odom, IMU, and optionally visual odometry → publishes fused /odometry/fused.
5	costmap_2d (nav2_costmap_2d) – global_costmap & local_costmap	Lifecycle	Builds static + dynamic obstacle layers from map, laser, and robot footprint.
6	planner_server (nav2_planner)	Lifecycle	Generates a global path (nav_msgs/Path) from start to goal using plugins (e.g., SmacPlannerHybrid).
7	controller_server (nav2_controller)	Lifecycle	Tracks the global path locally, outputs velocity commands (/cmd_vel).
8	bt_navigator (nav2_bt_navigator)	Lifecycle	Executes a behavior tree mission (navigate to goal, retry, cancel, recovery).
9	lifecycle_manager (nav2_lifecycle_manager)	Lifecycle	Starts/stops the whole Nav2 stack in the correct order.
10	goal_pose_server (custom)	Stateless / composable	Exposes a service /set_goal_pose (or action) that other UI/mission nodes call.
11	diff_drive_controller (nav2_controller/ros2_control driver)	Stateless	Subscribes to /cmd_vel, converts to wheel joint commands (/cmd_vel_left, /cmd_vel_right).
12	diagnostics_aggregator (diagnostics)	Stateless	Collects /diagnostics from all nodes, publishes /diagnostics.
13	safety_stop (custom)	Stateless	Monitors emergency topics (/estop, bumper, watchdog) → publishes zero velocity on /cmd_vel with higher QoS.
14	tf2_ros static_transform_publisher	Stateless	Publishes static transforms: map → odom, base_link → laser, base_link → wheel_left/right.
15	rviz2 (visualisation)	UI	Subscribes to map, pose, path, costmaps, laser, etc. (not part of runtime).
All nodes are launched via a single composable launch file (nav2_bringup.launch.py) that places the heavy weight nodes (map_server, amcl, planner, controller, bt_navigator, costmap) in a container for low latency intra process comms.
