4. End to End Data Flow
Below is the step by step path from raw sensors to motor actuation, annotated with the responsible node at each stage.
1.	LiDAR driver → laser_filter_node
•	Raw packets → sensor_msgs/LaserScan on /scan_raw.
•	laser_filter_node removes out of range points, applies a median filter, republishes filtered scan on /scan.
2.	Wheel encoders → diff_drive_controller (or a low level driver)
•	Publishes raw wheel odometry (/odom_raw).
3.	Fusion (robot_localization)
•	Subscribes to /odom_raw and (optionally) /imu/data.
•	Runs an EKF → publishes /odometry/fused (high rate, low latency).
4.	Localization (amcl)
•	Subscribes to /scan and /odometry/fused.
•	Uses the static map (/map) to compute a posterior over robot pose.
•	Publishes /amcl_pose (best estimate) and /particlecloud.
5.	Transform Tree
•	amcl also publishes a dynamic transform map → odom (the “localization offset”).
•	Static transforms: map → base_link, base_link → laser, base_link → wheel_left/right.
6.	Costmap Construction
•	Global Costmap: builds from static map + robot footprint → /global_costmap.
•	Local Costmap: builds from latest /scan, robot footprint, and dynamic obstacles → /local_costmap.
7.	Goal Reception
•	UI or mission planner calls /set_goal_pose (service) or sends a NavigateToPose action to /navigate_to_pose.
•	goal_pose_server validates and forwards the pose to the bt_navigator behavior tree (node 8).
8.	Behavior Tree (bt_navigator)
•	Starts a NavigateToPose BT which orchestrates the following sub tasks:
a. Planner → request global path (/plan).
b. Controller → follow the path while monitoring local costmap.
c. Recovery → if controller fails, invoke recovery behaviors (clear costmap, rotate in place, etc.).
9.	Planner (planner_server)
•	Receives start pose (from /amcl_pose) and goal pose.
•	Queries the global costmap, runs hybrid A* / Dijkstra → publishes /plan (nav_msgs/Path).
10.	Controller (controller_server)
•	Subscribes to /plan, /odometry/fused, /local_costmap.
•	Runs a trajectory controller (e.g., DWB, Regulated Pure Pursuit).
•	Emits a velocity command on /cmd_vel at ~20 Hz.
11.	Safety Stop (parallel)
•	Monitors /estop, bumper topics, and a watchdog on /cmd_vel.
•	If any condition triggers, it overwrites the command with a zero Twist (higher QoS) to ensure immediate stop.
12.	Diff Drive Driver (diff_drive_controller)
•	Receives /cmd_vel → splits into left/right wheel velocities.
•	Publishes wheel command topics (/cmd_vel_left, /cmd_vel_right) which are translated to the motor controller (CAN, serial, etc.).
13.	Motor Controllers → Motors
•	Low level firmware drives the wheels, closes the loop with encoders (feeding back to step 2).
14.	Feedback Loop
•	Wheel encoders → step 2 → step 3 → step 4 → … continues at 50 100 Hz, giving the system a tight closed loop.
15.	Diagnostics & Visualization
•	Each node emits diagnostic messages → diagnostics_aggregator → /diagnostics.
•	RViz subscribes to map, costmaps, laser, pose, path, and diagnostics for operator monitoring.
