7. Summary Checklist (copy paste for project README)
•	 Robot description (URDF + static TFs) – includes LiDAR frame and wheel joints.
•	 Map (.pgm/.yaml) placed in maps/.
•	 Launch nav2_bringup.launch.py (composable) with lifecycle manager.
•	 Parameters tuned (nav2_params.yaml, amcl_params.yaml, ekf.yaml).
•	 Goal interface (/navigate_to_pose action) exposed to UI/mission planner.
•	 Safety stop node subscribed to /estop and publishing override /cmd_vel.
•	 Diagnostics aggregated and visualised in RViz/rqt_robot_monitor.
•	 CI runs launch_testing with Gazebo to verify navigation to a series of random goals.
With the above architecture the robot will:
1.	Localise reliably on a known map using AMCL.
2.	Plan a collision free global trajectory to any user provided goal.
3.	Track that trajectory while reacting to dynamic obstacles via the local costmap.
4.	Stop safely instantly if an emergency condition occurs.
All components are modular, lifecycle aware, and composable, making the system easy to extend (e.g., add a 3 D depth camera, SLAM for unknown environments, or multi robot coordination) while keeping the real time control loop tight enough for a differential drive platform.

